# Line endings belong to the repository, not to each machine's git config.
#
# Added before the first push. The initial commit was made on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true, which printed "LF will be replaced by CRLF" for ~500 files: with no
# .gitattributes, what lands in a working copy depends on whoever checked it out. That is
# how a whole-file diff appears later for no reason, and it would also split this repo
# from CI, which checks out on Linux.
#
# text=auto eol=lf: git normalises to LF in the object store and checks out LF everywhere,
# including Windows. Every editor in use here handles LF, and the toolchain is Node.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts that genuinely need CRLF. cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only batch files.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binaries: never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.gif binary
*.heic binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.wasm binary
*.zip binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.traineddata binary

# Generated and vendored, so a diff is noise rather than review.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated
